[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The board reads the whole canon and cannot mutate it

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SDOC-BOARD-MVP-READS-WHOLE-CANON
TITLE: The board reads the whole canon and cannot mutate it
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The board presents every node and every resolved Parent or Child declaration
loaded from the canon, in each of its views. It offers no filter, no editor, no
mutation endpoint and no write-back path: selection, pan, zoom, table queries
and inspection are reading actions only.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ported 2026-09-01 from the codex spike branch (feat/strictdoc-trial-codex),
where it governed the board spike alone; the merged app extends it over the
Perspective view. The known cost of "every node": the whole-canon canvas is
denser than a person can read (operator, 2026-09-01). WORK-BOARD-FILTER-MODEL
owns deciding the filter model, and this requirement's no-filter clause is
expected to be superseded by what it decides.
<<<
